# Lead, 2026-09-28: the Qwen3.8 form of dma-dram-share.card, the one q38stream is decided on. The
# prefill design (q38pfd) streams the hot experts over a pinned staging ring while the host union
# computes the rest; its pp4096 band (1,559-1,663 tok/s, lcg, A6000) assumes the copy holds 26.28 GB/s
# beside the union. Unlike V4.1's engine:6 (136 GB/s, at the DRAM ceiling), Qwen3.8's union at 10
# columns an expert is compute-bound, 62-85 GB/s [derived, q38pfd §3], so U + 3C fits under ~145 GB/s
# with C near the link rate: predict C 20..26 and U within 10 % of its alone value.
# Wall [derived]: build 1-5 min, 4 rounds x 3 arms x ~40 s plus the copies alone, 10-15 min.
kind: profile
question: beside Qwen3.8's compute-bound host union, does the streaming design's staged copy hold the
  link rate?
term: C_staged, the median over rounds of h2d_probe staged-loop's GB/s (64 MiB pinned chunks, ring 4,
  4 fill threads, A6000) over each arm-round of bench_v41_host --time --arms union5:8x40u0.1 (32 experts
  x 10 columns) at 28 threads, Qwen3.8 UD-Q4_K_XL, beside it (dma-dram-share.sh's summary `staged ... C=`)
unit: GB/s
predict: 20..26
condition: BLOOMERY_MODEL=qwen4exp BLOOMERY_BOX_ENV='BLOOMERY_LEASE_CARD=docs/cards/dma-dram-share-q38.card'
  just time-dma-dram --arms union5:8x40u0.1 --rounds 4, one lease; the same admissibility, pinning,
  copy-alone and witness reads as dma-dram-share.card; U_alone printed beside U_with so the union's loss
  is read too
decide-in: spec q38stream at the q38pfd flow (c) rates, the ring pinned-staged, k(U) from q38-union.card's
  measured t(m)
decide-below: re-derive flow (c)'s k(U) with the measured C and k before q38stream is spec'd; try the
  L3-sized ring (--chunk 4194304) once
decide-above: not reachable (the link is 26.28): a reading above 26.5 is an instrument fault; read the
  runner's intervals before anything else
